  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/web-messaging.html#dom-window-postmessage isn't explicit about what to do when the target is, for example, a sandbox iframe without `allow-same-origin` whose document has an opaque origin serialized as the string `'null'`. In this case, it seems to make sense to be able to do this:\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\ntarget.postMessage(data, 'null');\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut this seems to fail step 5 in the above link as `'null'` cannot be parsed as an URL.\r\n\r\nShould we allow `targetOrigin` to be the string `\"null\"`? Both Chrome and Firefox don't allow it at the moment and will throw an error. The only workaround I'm aware of is to use the wildcard `*`, which seems more dangerous than using `\"null\"`.",
